///| Loop #90: an interactive SFTP client, one request at a time.
///
/// A separate package from `src/sftp` for the same reason `src/sftp` is a
/// separate package from `src/sshclient`: the protocol (framing, builders,
/// parsers) is one thing and the way it is driven is another. `src/sftp`
/// own `SftpSession` is the *scripted* driver (a whole op list up front,
/// which is what a known-answer test wants); this is the *interactive* one
/// (`stat`, look, decide, ask again), which is what `scp` wants.
import {
  "openssh/openssh_moonbit/src/sftp",
}

pkgtype(kind: "library")
